WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Tesla added a trick-or-treat mode that plays spooky sounds and lights when visitors approach the car. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 649. European Registrations, the German Cybertruck Decision, and fsd in Bratislava are the next stops, then first principles. Owners switch it on from toybox, then Halloween mode, then trick-or-treat, Tesla said, the control lives on the in-car touchscreen. The company posted a teaser video the same day warning trick-or-treaters to beware.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:37.752
Air. Major EU markets recorded Tesla registrations at a record high, according to NAI 500. The report

00:00:37.752 --> 00:00:43.052
tracks volume growth across those markets. Chinese electric vehicle makers showed a larger

00:00:43.052 --> 00:00:48.910
presence in the same data. The analysis flags competitive pressure in the region. German

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:54.270
regulators denied the cyber truck's certain road exemptions, the cooldown reports. They

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:59.190
cited the front end design over pedestrian safety. The decision blocks those operating

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:03.550
exemptions. It affects the truck's path to broader European market access.

00:01:04.721 --> 00:01:09.901
Local sent FSD down Bratislava's steep narrow streets, inside EVs reports.

00:01:10.741 --> 00:01:14.841
Testors ran tight urban routes and elevation changes in the Slovak capital.

00:01:15.381 --> 00:01:18.441
The system handled some complex maneuvers without intervention.

00:01:19.121 --> 00:01:22.201
Drivers still took over multiple times when signage was missed.

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:29.152
Switzerland remains outside the FSD rollout, Tesla Mag reports. Nine countries currently

00:01:29.152 --> 00:01:34.612
allow the system. The Swiss Federal Road's Office confirmed no formal submission had been received.

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:41.072
Tesla has secured approvals in other European nations. Robotaxi riders in Houston reported

00:01:41.072 --> 00:01:47.012
unexpected detours as the service area grew according to business insider. Those routes added

00:01:47.012 --> 00:01:52.932
time to trips. The operating zone continues to expand. The fleet stayed limited relative to that

00:01:52.932 --> 00:01:59.213
larger area. Tesla called for higher road user charges on combustion engine vehicles in Australia.

00:01:59.213 --> 00:02:00.693
The Australian reports.

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:05.033
The company said the charge should not simply replace fuel excise revenue.

00:02:05.613 --> 00:02:09.293
That position was set out in submissions on Australian transport policy.

00:02:10.316 --> 00:02:16.616
Next-generation roadster rendering show a thruster gauge that reads to 5,500 psi, according

00:02:16.616 --> 00:02:17.516
to tech insider.

00:02:18.116 --> 00:02:21.016
The interface uses retro-futuristic styling cues.

00:02:21.536 --> 00:02:23.836
Those screens are tied to the Roadster program.

00:02:23.836 --> 00:02:30.331
Ford's Model E Electric Vehicle Division posted a $1.1 billion loss in the third quarter,

00:02:30.851 --> 00:02:32.331
drive Tesla Canada reports.

00:02:32.971 --> 00:02:36.751
Profitability metrics still showed sequential gains from prior periods.

00:02:37.231 --> 00:02:40.271
The results cover Ford's dedicated EV business unit.

00:02:41.221 --> 00:02:46.141
A clean technical writer says FSD now gives far fewer reasons to intervene or complain.

00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:52.481
Seven years ago, that writer paid Tesla $6,000 for a permanent subscription on a new Model 3.

00:02:52.481 --> 00:02:58.501
At the time, the system would navigate automatically on limited access highways, mostly interstates,

00:02:58.781 --> 00:02:59.381
and little else.

00:02:59.861 --> 00:03:04.441
The same writer now drives a 2026 base model Y with FSD.

00:03:05.201 --> 00:03:07.521
Fewer interventions are required on city streets.

00:03:08.061 --> 00:03:11.801
The system handles more scenarios without prompting the driver to take over.

00:03:12.781 --> 00:03:18.941
Proposed legislation would restore the federal EV tax credit and raise it to $15,000, notebook

00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:19.801
check reports.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:25.201
units. The change would apply to qualifying electric vehicles. Tesla models stand to benefit

00:03:25.201 --> 00:03:31.801
if the bill advances. Tesla opened a new supercharger in Norwood, Ontario, Drive Tesla Canada

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:37.461
reports. The site adds capacity along eastern Ontario routes. It joins the growing North

00:03:37.461 --> 00:03:43.832
American network. The location supports longer trips between major centers. CyberCab production

00:03:43.832 --> 00:03:50.092
is being lined up to use half the factory space. Mario Naufal set on X. The unboxed process

00:03:50.092 --> 00:03:54.012
as builds and test different sections of the car separately before they come together.

00:03:54.552 --> 00:03:58.652
Final assembly is down to 25 stations with 78% automation.

00:03:59.352 --> 00:04:01.432
Build steps and test steps are kept apart.

00:04:02.551 --> 00:04:05.491
Cameras scale better than LiDAR for spotting small animals.

00:04:06.111 --> 00:04:11.711
TSLA Amming argued on X. A cat far down the road only catches a handful of laser points.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:15.431
Better cameras and software can go out to every car overnight.

00:04:16.151 --> 00:04:19.431
LiDAR hardware cannot match that fleet-wide distribution speed.

00:04:19.431 --> 00:04:24.963
Robotaxi live activities got a new look in a post on the Tesla Motors subreddit.

00:04:25.563 --> 00:04:28.503
Riders see refreshed interface elements during active trips.

00:04:29.003 --> 00:04:31.423
The chain shows up in recent software builds.

00:04:31.963 --> 00:04:37.543
Seoul's Central District Court dismissed a lawsuit from 89 Tesla owners seeking FSD refunds.

00:04:38.083 --> 00:04:42.303
SBS reports the owner said the option failed to deliver driverless operation.

00:04:42.883 --> 00:04:48.503
The court treated the purchase as an indeterminate contract tied to regulatory approval and technical progress,

00:04:48.503 --> 00:04:54.863
so missing level 5 capability did not breach the terms. Tesla said the system is not complete in

00:04:54.863 --> 00:05:00.663
Korea, and that buyers accepted that uncertainty. The option has been priced between 6 million and

00:05:00.663 --> 00:05:08.823
10 million won since 2017. 98 owners originally filed, 9 withdrew, and owners had argued the option

00:05:08.823 --> 00:05:15.751
should not have been sold if full autonomy could not be guaranteed. BYD now employs 1.02 million

00:05:15.751 --> 00:05:23.131
people. That headcount tops Toyota, GM, Ford, and Tesla put together. From the end of 2025,

00:05:23.571 --> 00:05:31.031
it added roughly 150,000 people in 10 months. Of that wave, 120,000 sit in research and development

00:05:31.031 --> 00:05:38.311
on batteries, motors, electronic controls, and semiconductors. 960,000 staff remain in China,

00:05:38.311 --> 00:05:47.891
and 60,000 work overseas. Tesla's latest reported head count stands at 134,785 worldwide. Toyota

00:05:47.891 --> 00:06:00.471
reported 390,927 employees as of March 2026. Ford ended 2025 with 169,000, and GM with 156,000.

00:06:01.051 --> 00:06:06.751
Vertical integration explains much of the gap. BYD makes key parts in-house across batteries,

00:06:06.751 --> 00:06:11.551
chips, and motors, and draws workers from an electronics contract manufacturing

00:06:11.551 --> 00:06:16.431
arm that alone employed 165,000 at the end of 2025.

00:06:17.111 --> 00:06:21.971
That structure inflates total employment without a direct link to vehicles built per person.

00:06:22.651 --> 00:06:27.591
Tesla's smaller workforce focuses more narrowly on vehicle assembly, energy products,

00:06:27.871 --> 00:06:32.751
and software, so raw headcount masks what each employee contributes to the finished product.

00:06:32.751 --> 00:06:41.871
Volkswagen Group reported 662,942 employees at the end of 2025, sitting between BYD and

00:06:41.871 --> 00:06:49.251
the US and Japanese groups. BYD's hiring spree followed a drop to 869,600 at the close

00:06:49.251 --> 00:06:57.211
of 2025, after earlier peaks above 900,000. A company that carries 170,000 more employees

00:06:57.211 --> 00:07:02.211
than its nearest rivals must spread those costs across higher volumes or accept lower

00:07:02.211 --> 00:07:07.631
returns per vehicle. Tesla keeps the employee-based smaller while scaling software and energy

00:07:07.631 --> 00:07:12.671
businesses that do not need the same physical labor intensity, which may preserve margin

00:07:12.671 --> 00:07:17.311
flexibility even if absolute production stays lower than a fully integrated rival.

00:07:18.091 --> 00:07:25.211
BYD sold about 4.6 million vehicles last year with 869,600 employees at year end,

00:07:25.731 --> 00:07:31.591
equating to 5.3 vehicles per worker. The headcount gap does not automatically translate to

00:07:31.591 --> 00:07:35.871
superior competitiveness when productivity metrics differ across business scopes.

